  "reasoning": "The claim is accurate. In a widely cited 2023 study by Daniel Martin Katz, Michael Bommarito, et al. (\"GPT-4 Passes the Bar Exam\"), OpenAI's GPT-4 was evaluated on the Uniform Bar Examination (UBE) and achieved a total scaled score of 297. Passing thresholds in all UBE jurisdictions range from 260 to 272, meaning the model comfortably passed in every jurisdiction. While OpenAI initially reported this score placed the model around the 90th percentile, subsequent peer-reviewed critique (e.g., Martinez, 2023) clarified that compared to first-time test-takers who passed the July exam, the score corresponds to approximately the 68th to 69th percentile. Under either evaluation, a score in the ~68th percentile is definitively above average (the 50th percentile).",
